1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,629
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:15,765
<i>Don't bother coming back</i>
<i>until you have Arthur's body.</i>

3
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:18,560
<i>I'll pay you whatever you want</i>
<i>as long as you kill that bastard.</i>

4
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:22,272
<i>What I want to know</i>
<i>is who was behind this.</i>

5
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,983
<i>Do you think it's Diego?</i>

6
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:27,027
<i>That bastard.</i>

7
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,903
<i>You think I don't know what you did?</i>

8
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:32,407
<i>You had Arthur kidnap Ivy.</i>
<i>You can't stop our wedding.</i>

9
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:35,744
<i>I'll put a stop to all your plans.</i>

10
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,203
<i>-Let's go. We need to leave.</i>
<i>-Hon?</i>

11
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:38,913
<i>Let's go to Hong Kong.</i>
<i>We will get married there.</i>

12
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:40,415
<i>Let's start a new life somewhere.</i>

13
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:41,666
<i>Hon, relax.</i>

14
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,543
<i>If someone dares to try</i>
<i>to stop our wedding,</i>

15
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:45,211
<i>I won't let them.</i>

16
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,422
<i>Boss Jaguar says the Ardientes</i>
<i>are hot on our trail.</i>

17
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:49,340
<i>He also heard that Julio Ardiente</i>

18
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,925
<i>asked a private army to hunt us down.</i>

19
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:53,636
<i>But we won't let them intimidate us.</i>

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,513
<i>We'll continue with our casino operations.</i>

21
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,015
[Jepoy] <i>Now that I'm back,</i>

22
00:00:57,098 --> 00:01:01,186
<i>I will make you suffer much worse</i>
<i>than I did back then.</i>

23
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:03,313
<i>I will use Jaguar's weapons</i>

24
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:05,982
<i>to wipe out the entire Ardiente clan!</i>

25
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:08,860
<i>We have been preparing for the forthcoming</i>

26
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:12,280
<i>Aguas-Ardiente royal wedding.</i>

27
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:16,743
<i>It is finally going to happen</i>
<i>a week from today.</i>

28
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:19,454
-<i>No! No! No! No!</i>
-[pounding on table]

29
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:22,499
[Raul] <i>Once we reach the casino,</i>
<i>go straight to the cashiers.</i>

30
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:24,417
<i>Get everything you can get.</i>

31
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:27,337
<i>Don't shoot unless necessary.</i>
<i>I want this to be a clean job.</i>

32
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,964
<i>Remember, we're going outside Ardiente.</i>

33
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,883
<i>It isn't our turf.</i>

34
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:32,967
[Jepoy] <i>They're tailing us.</i>

35
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:36,137
<i>Julio Ardiente's men.</i>
<i>It isn't safe to do this now.</i>

36
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,932
[Julio] <i>Ivy Aguas is not fooling us.</i>

37
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:41,810
<i>We are fooling her!</i>

38
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:45,772
<i>When we have sucked Ivy Aguas</i>
<i>bone-dry of her money,</i>

39
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,899
<i>and her good public image,</i>

40
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:50,068
<i>then she can be my present to you,</i>

41
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:52,654
<i>and you can do with her whatever you want.</i>

42
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:55,865
[man] <i>If you hadn't warned our boss,</i>
<i>we would've gotten into bigger trouble.</i>

43
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,867
[Jepoy] <i>Now that I have money and weapons,</i>

44
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:01,079
<i>I will stop your wedding</i>
<i>with bullets, Arnaldo.</i>

45
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,334
<i>And now, everyone,</i>

46
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:07,293
-here he is!
-Hon?

47
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,379
As you can see, the man of the hour

48
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:11,548
-has arrived.
-[Ivy] Hon.

49
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:12,799
-You look beautiful.
-It's Mayor Arnaldo.

50
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:14,342
-Thank you.
-And of course,

51
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:17,887
we shouldn't forget about
Congressman Julio Ardiente!

52
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:20,223
<i>He's also here, everyone.</i>

53
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:22,225
-[Julio] <i>Hello. Hello.</i>
-[Phomella] <i>Hello, sir. Hello.</i>

54
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:23,810
-[chuckling]
-How are you?

55
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:28,773
This place looks like a bridal shop!

56
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:29,858
[chuckles]

57
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,734
[Julio] Look, don't get me wrong.

58
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:33,653
Uh, not that I'm complaining.

59
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,238
Hello, everyone!

60
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:37,574
<i>Let me ask you a question.</i>

61
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:38,950
<i>Are you all excited</i>

62
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:42,162
<i>for the forthcoming wedding</i>
<i>of the century?</i>

63
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,705
[all] Yes, Congressman!

64
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,875
That's nice to hear. Viva Ardiente.

65
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,126
[Arnaldo] Viva Ardiente.

66
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,210
You know,

67
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:53,923
the future of this family
has never been brighter.

68
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:57,093
And it can only get brighter
in the days to come!

69
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:59,220
[chuckles] Yes, Grandpa.
And it's all because of you.

70
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,222
No! Come on, Arnaldo.

71
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,557
Congressman…

72
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:09,230
Instead of "Congressman,"
may I call you "Grandpa" now?

73
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:10,899
Of course!

74
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:14,777
Grandpa, Arnaldo and I
would like to thank you

75
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:19,532
for giving us your blessing
to get married right away.

76
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:23,328
Well, if you put it that way.

77
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,997
You know, the truth of the matter is,

78
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:30,418
the first time I saw you two together,

79
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:33,504
I knew right away in my heart of hearts

80
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:36,883
that you were meant to be.

81
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,301
-Aww, hon.
-[chuckles]

82
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:41,804
[Phomella] <i>Wow! Would you look at that?</i>

83
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:44,766
<i>It won't be long before Miss Ivy</i>

84
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:48,853
<i>becomes the new queen</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente!</i>

85
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,230
-[Julio chuckles]
-[Phomella] Oh, my.

86
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,522
<i>We are all very excited.</i>

87
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:53,399
<i>And I'm sure you all feel the same.</i>

88
00:03:54,692 --> 00:03:56,569
-[Emilia] Hey, Phomella!
-[Phomella] Oh!

89
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,196
-Ms. Emilia, hello!
-[Emilia] Hi.

90
00:03:58,279 --> 00:03:59,155
-It's nice
-How are you?

91
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:00,490
-to have you back here!
-Hello!

92
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,158
-It's been a long time!
-Hello.

93
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,827
<i>Hi, dear friends! Hi!</i>

94
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:08,456
You know, Phomella, my father
was so right when he said

95
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:11,501
that Ivy and Arnaldo
are destined to be together.

96
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:12,669
-[Julio] Yeah.
-Can you just imagine

97
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:14,128
their love story?

98
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:16,506
Ivy didn't even like Arnaldo

99
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,841
because, at that time,
Arnaldo was seeing Natalie.

100
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:20,009
-[laughing]
-[clears throat]

101
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:21,552
-Mama.
-Oh. I'm sorry.

102
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,972
<i>That was so awkward. Sorry. </i>[chuckles]

103
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,848
<i>But you know, as they say,</i>

104
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:28,393
<i>if two people really love each other,</i>

105
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:29,769
they will find each other in the end.

106
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:32,146
Look at you now! You're getting married.

107
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,899
Isn't that exciting, Auntie?

108
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:38,486
And, you know, I've prepared
something for both of you.

109
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:41,072
Um, to prove your love for each other,

110
00:04:41,155 --> 00:04:44,784
I prepared a prenuptial agreement

111
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:46,911
that both of you will sign, of course.

112
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:51,165
[gloomy music playing]

113
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,087
Uh…

114
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:58,006
Mama, I think we should talk
about this in private.

115
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:00,133
[laughs] Come on, Arnaldo.

116
00:05:00,216 --> 00:05:04,387
The public already saw the size
of my waistline earlier.

117
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,056
Besides, this is just to protect you.

118
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,433
-Come on.
-[forced chuckle]

119
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:11,561
<i>Protect me from what? From Ivy?</i>
<i>Are you kidding me?</i>

120
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:14,063
-[Emilia] <i>Come on!</i>
-[Julio] <i>Come on, Arnaldo.</i>

121
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:17,900
It's the millennium. The modern age.

122
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:21,195
It's normal to discuss these things.

123
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:24,866
Consider it. Won't your relationship

124
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:29,537
be stronger if you knew
that you were protected?

125
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:31,789
-[Emilia] Yeah.
-[Julio] I mean,

126
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,499
if the both of you are protected.

127
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,542
Mm-hmm.

128
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,086
Grandpa is right, hon.

129
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,881
With or without that prenuptial agreement,

130
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:42,759
my love for you will never change.

131
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:45,720
I love you so much!

132
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:46,929
-[Arnaldo] I love you too.
-[Emilia] Oh.

133
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,431
-<i>That's really sweet.</i>
-[applause on TV]

134
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:50,516
[Emilia] <i>Oh, gosh.</i>

135
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:52,268
<i>Wait, Ivy.</i>

136
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,645
Aren't you even going
to read the document?

137
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:57,356
Oh…

138
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:01,694
It says there that should you
and Arnaldo decide to separate,

139
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,571
one hundred percent of your assets

140
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:05,239
will go to Arnaldo.

141
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:11,162
[suspenseful music playing]

142
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:15,958
[woman] What?! All of it?!

143
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:24,133
One hundred percent?!
You are so greedy, Emilia!

144
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,721
[Jepoy] <i>Don't sign it, Ivy.</i>

145
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:31,265
[suspenseful music playing]

146
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:46,781
-Watch, Auntie.
-Hon, I love you so much.

147
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:48,783
I really do.

148
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:55,081
No amount of money can ever
compare to my love for you.

149
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:57,667
-[clears throat]
-That's why I will sign this.

150
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:01,420
Right now, while we're
in front of the camera.

151
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:05,299
This way, I can show Poblacion Ardiente,

152
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,927
Grandpa Julio, Mamita,

153
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:14,016
and Mama Emilia
just how much I love Arnaldo.

154
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:18,146
[suspenseful music intensifies]

155
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,449
[camera shutter clicks]

156
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:37,999
[suspenseful music playing]

157
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:56,309
Friends! As you can see, we are live!

158
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,936
The couple is signing a prenup agreement.

159
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:02,732
That's why I can really feel the love

160
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:06,819
<i>and trust this family has for each other.</i>

161
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:13,284
<i>As you can see, Miss Ivy really</i>
<i>loves her soon-to-be family.</i>

162
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:23,753
-[gloomy guitar music playing]
-[man] This is too much.

163
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:50,154
Auntie?

164
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:58,579
Diego, I promised Lily
that I would trust her plan.

165
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:04,877
But I can't allow those greedy
Ardientes to do this to her.

166
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:13,094
My goodness. Look at that.

167
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:14,178
[camera shutter clicks]

168
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,264
Miss Ivy signed it in front of you,

169
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:20,351
so you can see how much she truly loves

170
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:22,228
her soon-to-be family.

171
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:25,314
[suspenseful music playing]

172
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:26,399
[camera shutter clicks]

173
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:31,028
[Ivy] <i>I know that prenup was a trap.</i>

174
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:35,825
<i>You thought I would say no?</i>

175
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:39,745
<i>You are talking to Ivy Aguas.</i>

176
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:42,206
<i>And the person who will beat me</i>

177
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:46,085
<i>at my own game hasn't been born yet.</i>

178
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:50,131
[camera shutter clicks]

179
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:53,301
Diego, this is too dangerous.

180
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,891
Auntie, I understand you.

181
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:03,853
But the best way
we can help Lily right now

182
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:05,730
is by trusting her.

183
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,358
Auntie, your daughter
has been through so much.

184
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,402
She can take care of herself.

185
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:17,033
But for now, I will need your help.

186
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:21,621
We need to talk to all
the teachers here in Ardiente.

187
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:25,207
Let's convince them
to be steadfast and brave,

188
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,960
and to hold on to their principles.

189
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:30,212
We need to encourage them to be firm

190
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:31,672
in preparation for the upcoming elections,

191
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,341
so they won't be blinded
by the Ardientes' money,

192
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,718
or be threatened by their weapons.

193
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:36,802
Diego is right.

194
00:10:38,262 --> 00:10:40,640
Our teachers are the key
to having an honest election.

195
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,893
If that's the case,
we shouldn't waste more time.

196
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:47,146
Let's start acting before
the Ardientes beat us to it.

197
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:54,737
Look, Papa. She signed it.

198
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,739
I know and it's got me thinking.

199
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:01,369
Hon, you think your mother's happy now?

200
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:05,998
She thought I would back out
because of the prenup.

201
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:09,418
Of course not, Ivy. I'm the happiest.

202
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:13,506
Because your union is a match
made in Ardiente's heaven.

203
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:17,510
Indeed! I agree a hundred percent.

204
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:18,552
Mm-hmm.

205
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:22,348
Well, well, well, my son, Arnaldo.

206
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:27,228
After a long and difficult hunt,
you finally landed Miss Aguas.

207
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:32,274
Did Arnaldo catch me, or…

208
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:35,778
was it Arnaldo who fell into my trap?

209
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:37,238
[suspenseful music playing]

210
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:40,116
[Julio chuckles] Well, you know, Ivy,

211
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:42,785
it really doesn't matter who got who

212
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:47,164
because, after the wedding,
you will become an Ardiente.

213
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,542
A bona fide member of this family,

214
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:55,423
and what you own will basically
belong to Arnaldo too.

215
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,967
That's where we'll have
a problem, Congressman.

216
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:03,722
I'm selfish. What's mine is mine.

217
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:06,058
That's why Arnaldo…

218
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,562
belongs only to me.

219
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:10,813
Right, hon?

220
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:13,524
[suspenseful music playing]

221
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:15,609
[Emilia] I'm having a migraine, Papa.

222
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,028
-A severe one.
-[Julio mutters indistinctly]

223
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,578
[tense music playing]

224
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:49,435
[exhales]

225
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:56,066
Ivy, before I do forget,

226
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:58,402
kudos to you

227
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:03,032
for agreeing to that prenup,
which really surprised me.

228
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:08,537
I didn't expect you to just
agree to it just like that.

229
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:13,876
And, Arnaldo, if you're looking
for confirmation of true love,

230
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:17,880
what your wife-to-be here did

231
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:21,008
was clearly a statement of true love.

232
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,134
[Emilia] Mm-hmm.

233
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,639
That's because I really love Arnaldo.

234
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:31,685
Oh, and not to pressure the two of you…

235
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:37,566
I would like to have grandchildren
very, very soon.

236
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:40,361
-[forced chuckle]
-[Julio] Because…

237
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:45,616
I'd like to still be able to guide

238
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:49,662
and teach the future
Ardientes of this family

239
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:50,829
before I…

240
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:55,042
disappear into oblivion.

241
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:59,129
Don't say such morbid things, Papa.

242
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:02,258
Don't be like that.
And besides, it's too early.

243
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:06,011
Ivy wouldn't want
to ruin her figure, right?

244
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,555
[chuckles]

245
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:08,889
It's not about my figure, Emilia.

246
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:11,433
I don't mind it. It's just that…

247
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,644
I was thinking that after the wedding,

248
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:19,316
we should prioritize
securing Arnaldo's victory

249
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,734
in the elections.

250
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:23,237
I think that's more urgent, right?

251
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,866
Now you're talking like a true Ardiente.

252
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:28,033
[chuckles]

253
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,952
And you've got me thinking, Ivy.

254
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:33,497
Maybe in the next elections,

255
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,458
you should run for office.

256
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,172
You should go for Congress!

257
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:48,721
As for me, I can step down
and just run for mayor.

258
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:52,808
Of course, Arnaldo can run
for reelection as governor.

259
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:58,439
That way, we'll have
full control over Ardiente.

260
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:01,483
[Arnaldo] Brilliant idea, Grandpa.

261
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,277
Of course, I always have brilliant ideas.

262
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,403
He's right.

263
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:06,530
I can just switch political positions

264
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:08,949
-Wow. Great idea.
-with Ivy, then with Grandpa.

265
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,367
Yes.

266
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:13,329
Hold on. What about Emilia?

267
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:16,415
Won't she be running
for a position like before?

268
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:17,958
Oh, Mama?

269
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:21,962
Well, I'm sure every grandmother

270
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,839
is excited to take care
of her grandchildren.

271
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:24,882
[laughs]

272
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:26,258
[Julio] That's right. That's true.

273
00:15:26,842 --> 00:15:28,218
I'm sorry.

274
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,888
Hon, you're so mean.

275
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:34,058
A former governor turned babysitter?

276
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:36,727
[Julio] Hey, don't take that so lightly.

277
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:38,812
That's another royal title for her.

278
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:40,981
-That's right.
-Granny Lia.

279
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:43,275
It sounds like "Princess Leia."

280
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,902
-Granny Lia.
-[glass thuds]

281
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,321
Congressman, I don't think
it's a good idea

282
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:48,405
to leave her jobless.

283
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:52,326
Well, she can work for my company instead.

284
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:55,704
Don't worry, Emilia,
I'll be a kind boss. Trust me.

285
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:58,165
[fake chuckle] No, thank you, Ivy.

286
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,459
I still have other things
to keep me occupied.

287
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,670
Really? Like what?

288
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,798
You wouldn't want to know.
It involves violence.

289
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:07,508
Excuse me.

290
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:09,969
[tense music playing]

291
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:14,264
Oh, well. She got mad again.

292
00:16:14,348 --> 00:16:18,435
I guess I should go talk
to my future mother-in-law.

293
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:20,729
-[chuckles]
-Excuse me.

294
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:21,855
[Arnaldo] Go.

295
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,525
[Julio] Ah…

296
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,947
So, now you're drinking all by yourself?

297
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:33,826
No. I just tasted the wine.

298
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:37,079
Poor Emilia. I know you're jealous

299
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,748
because you won't be running
for any office.

300
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:42,793
I'm sorry if I'm slowly
stealing your place here

301
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:46,380
at the mansion, and in Poblacion Ardiente.

302
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:47,589
Sorry.

303
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:51,802
Me? Threatened by you taking my place?

304
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:52,886
[scoffs]

305
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:54,722
That will never happen, Ivy.

306
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:57,725
Remember, you're just a wife-to-be.

307
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,810
I'm the mother.

308
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:02,312
And that will never, ever change.

309
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:07,943
So, that means I will still be
the queen of Ardiente.

310
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,069
[chuckles]

311
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,739
I never really planned to steal

312
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:14,992
whatever place you thought
you had, Emilia.

313
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,870
But if you're going
to sabotage my wedding,

314
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,872
I'm telling you…

315
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:25,335
[suspenseful music playing]

316
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:26,628
I'm so scared.

317
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:29,423
You should be.

318
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:33,886
Hmm.

319
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:38,223
Hey, hon. Where's Mama?

320
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,351
Like I told you, she's sulking again.

321
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:47,316
What? Sulking? Who, me? Of course not.

322
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:52,321
Oh, you guys. You know,
I just got a bit emotional

323
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:55,365
because my son is about
to get married soon.

324
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:58,786
And I just realized something.

325
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,538
[sighs] Finally, Arnaldo,

326
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:04,416
you've found a woman who loves you,

327
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,710
and is ready to die for you.

328
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:10,255
And because of that, Ivy,

329
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:12,633
[sighs]

330
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:15,928
I'm going to throw you
a bridal shower party!

331
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:18,388
Just to show you how much I appreciate

332
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:21,225
all your efforts for Arnaldo.

333
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:25,437
I promise I'll make you happy!
Party! Party!

334
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,441
I'm looking forward to it.
A bridal shower?

335
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,901
-Yeah.
-[Ivy] Exciting.

336
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:32,528
-Mm-hmm.
-Thank you.

337
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:33,862
You're so sweet, Emilia.

338
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,030
I am.

339
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:38,742
-[Julio] So nice of you.
-Hon…

340
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:40,869
It's okay.

341
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:46,708
I'm sure Emilia wouldn't hurt me
or have me killed.

342
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:51,004
I mean, I'm confident
she wants us to get married.

343
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,339
Right, Emilia?

344
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:56,301
Of course! In fact, I'm so excited!

345
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:57,553
Right, Auntie?

346
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:00,305
I can tell.

347
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:01,723
[Emilia] Yeah.

348
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:05,018
[tense music playing]

349
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,317
[Marlon] Double-check the particulars.

350
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:14,278
Our expenses might have been doubling.

351
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,988
-Okay, sir.
-Thanks.

352
00:19:17,781 --> 00:19:20,075
Batch, Arnaldo and Ivy's wedding

353
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:21,577
will generate enormous publicity.

354
00:19:21,910 --> 00:19:25,164
We might lose if they garner
sympathy from the people.

355
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:27,916
We'll have to act on their wedding day.

356
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,627
Let's gather more people.

357
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:35,799
We have to expand our network,
starting with the teachers.

358
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:38,719
You're right, Batch.
We can start with the teachers.

359
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:42,931
[Arnaldo] Here you go, Grandpa.

360
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,725
Thank you, grandson.

361
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:48,187
Thanks for supporting me and Ivy today.

362
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,563
-It means a lot to me.
-[glasses clink]

363
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:54,735
For you, son, I'll do anything.
Which reminds me.

364
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:59,531
That's why I prepared a surprise
for you later on.

365
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:03,410
To celebrate your last time being single,

366
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:06,914
I'm throwing you a stag party

367
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:10,292
on the same day as Ivy's bridal shower.

368
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:14,087
Hey, Papa, I heard you talking
about a stag party.

369
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:15,214
Am I invited?

370
00:20:15,797 --> 00:20:17,591
Of course not, Raul.

371
00:20:17,674 --> 00:20:20,302
Knowing you, if you were invited,

372
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:24,431
you'd just steal whichever woman
I prepared for my grandson.

373
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:27,017
I'd feel bad for Emilia.

374
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,518
[Raul] Well, then,

375
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,730
you go have fun, son.

376
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:35,234
Papa, thank you so much
for devoting time to my son.

377
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:36,985
Anytime. For him.

378
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:41,823
By the way, Emilia mentioned
something about you

379
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:47,746
paying off Jaguar's henchman.
And that Jaguar found out.

380
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:52,042
I bet he's mad, Papa.
And that he's out for revenge.

381
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:56,713
What if he sends more than
just a few ants next time?

382
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:57,798
Right?

383
00:20:58,215 --> 00:21:01,843
He might send the big guns.
You should be careful.

384
00:21:02,844 --> 00:21:04,680
[tense music playing]

385
00:21:05,347 --> 00:21:07,224
Such arrogance.

386
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:17,150
I don't like this, Emilia.

387
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,819
I've repeatedly warned you.

388
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:22,155
Your actions will only
get you into trouble!

389
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:27,411
Well, Auntie, I'd rather die than see Ivy

390
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:29,746
steal everything I own.

391
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:32,791
And asking or paying someone
to do it for me

392
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:36,253
is not working anymore,
so I'd rather do it myself.

393
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:39,006
That way, I'll take her life
with my own, two hands--

394
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:41,341
Then you better do
it successfully, Emilia!

395
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:44,469
Not only will Ivy hit you again,

396
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:46,972
but Arnaldo and Julio might even kill you.

397
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:51,184
I'm not afraid of Papa
and Arnaldo anymore, Auntie.

398
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:53,312
Because I have someone on my side

399
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:55,480
who is more than willing to make me,

400
00:21:55,564 --> 00:21:57,649
not just a queen, but a king.

401
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:02,321
[suspenseful music playing]

402
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:22,090
[cell phone ringing]

403
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,386
Emilia.

404
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:29,014
[in distorted voice] <i>I'm sick</i>
<i>and tired of your voice.</i>

405
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:32,934
I want to see your beauty.

406
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:35,687
Then I called at the right time

407
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:37,564
because I'll be needing you tonight.

408
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:38,774
What for?

409
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:43,028
I'm throwing a bridal shower
for my future daughter-in-law.

410
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:46,948
Maybe you can let me borrow
some of your macho men

411
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:50,368
to entertain my daughter-in-law,
Ivy Aguas.

412
00:22:50,994 --> 00:22:57,042
What if I go there
and entertain them myself?

413
00:22:57,125 --> 00:23:00,045
<i>Including your future daughter-in-law.</i>

414
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,464
She might end up marrying me instead.

415
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:03,840
Are you trying to make me jealous?

416
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:07,427
Well, I can't blame you
because, first of all,

417
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:10,722
<i>I've heard that Miss Aguas is beautiful.</i>

418
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:13,225
And I'm handsome, so why not?

419
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:15,393
You're annoying, Jaguar.

420
00:23:15,477 --> 00:23:17,813
You know, you really do remind me
of my husband.

421
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:19,648
Never mind, don't come here.

422
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:22,984
Wow. You really do like to sulk, Emilia.

423
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:26,696
<i>Don't worry. All the wounds</i>
<i>caused by your husband</i>

424
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,990
will eventually heal.

425
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:31,326
<i>I'll heal them with my kisses.</i>

426
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:32,536
[chuckles]

427
00:23:32,619 --> 00:23:38,500
Well, I'll really know that you're sincere
if you send some of your men over tonight.

428
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:42,212
[tense music playing]

429
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:50,428
-[Diego] Come and eat.
-[Camia] Thanks for your time.

430
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:51,847
-Good afternoon.
-Here's the food.

431
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:52,764
There you go.

432
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:54,850
-This is Ms. Loring's specialty.
-[Pandoy] Yes, it is!

433
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,226
-So delicious.
-I got it from you.

434
00:23:56,309 --> 00:23:57,435
[laughter]

435
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:59,062
[Loring] Please sit down.

436
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:02,190
-[Camia] Have a seat.
-Uh, good afternoon to you all.

437
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:04,568
Thank you very much for coming here.

438
00:24:05,068 --> 00:24:06,778
What's the agenda of this meeting?

439
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:12,534
Uh, we believe we need teachers
like you for a fair election.

440
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,494
I used to be a teacher too,

441
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:16,580
and I also served as a poll worker.

442
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:19,666
I know how important your role is

443
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:22,294
in guarding the votes of the people.

444
00:24:22,711 --> 00:24:24,087
[Diego] That's why we thought

445
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:27,382
of establishing an alliance
of teachers for fair elections.

446
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:31,553
Let's stop the cheating.
We want to protect you

447
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:34,931
from bribery, harassment,
and intimidation.

448
00:24:35,015 --> 00:24:36,558
Thank you, sir.

449
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:39,186
At least now, we are assured

450
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:42,480
that somebody will protect us
in the coming elections.

451
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:43,481
Right, everyone?

452
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:44,566
-That's right.
-That's right.

453
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:47,944
And you can trust that we will protect you

454
00:24:48,486 --> 00:24:51,698
as long as we help each other
strive for change.

455
00:24:51,781 --> 00:24:53,658
[in unison] For a new Ardiente!

456
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:56,203
Sir, if I may.

457
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:59,706
We have a teaching drive
in Barangay Siete.

458
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:03,460
Maybe you'd like to come?
I hope you can help us out.

459
00:25:03,543 --> 00:25:05,712
-[Marlon] Go, Batch.
-Oh. Of course.

460
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:08,840
We'll bring more aid
for the kids there too.

461
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:10,133
You're really impressive, sir.

462
00:25:10,217 --> 00:25:12,594
You really are bringing great change.

463
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:15,639
This is for our beloved
Poblacion Ardiente.

464
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:19,601
We'll all come together
for a new Ardiente.

465
00:25:19,684 --> 00:25:22,062
Diego for a new Ardiente!

466
00:25:22,145 --> 00:25:24,689
-Diego!
-Everyone, for a new Ardiente!

467
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:25,774
-Diego!
-Diego!

468
00:25:25,857 --> 00:25:29,819
-For a new Ardiente!
-[all chanting] Diego! Diego!

469
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:36,910
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

470
00:25:37,702 --> 00:25:39,704
[man 4] Looks like we're going
to be strippers tonight.

471
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:41,122
[laughter]

472
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:43,291
Dude, it's just one night.

473
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:46,211
Let's just humor our boss.
He'll be paying us well.

474
00:25:46,294 --> 00:25:49,923
I agree. Dude, show us some of your moves.

475
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:50,882
[chuckles]

476
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:54,469
I wish we were going
to Arnaldo's stag party.

477
00:25:54,552 --> 00:25:56,930
Our boss would send girls over, for sure.

478
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,181
-[man 5] Yeah.
-[man 4] But instead,

479
00:25:58,265 --> 00:25:59,808
we're going to a bridal shower.

480
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:03,853
[village chairman] Everyone!

481
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:05,063
The man we're waiting for has arrived!

482
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:06,856
-[chanting] Diego!
-[chairman] Diego Torillo!

483
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:10,694
[kids chanting] Diego Torillo!

484
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:12,821
Good afternoon, everyone!

485
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:16,574
Thank you for accepting our invitation.

486
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:18,410
Helping every village in Ardiente

487
00:26:18,493 --> 00:26:19,995
is part of our program.

488
00:26:20,578 --> 00:26:23,915
So, kids, are you ready for today's games?

489
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,834
[kids] Yes!

490
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:27,836
-Let's go!
-[kids shouting]

491
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,464
[feel-good music playing]

492
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:37,262
[no audible dialogue]

493
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:52,444
[feel-good music playing]

494
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:17,260
[feel-good music playing]

495
00:27:34,694 --> 00:27:37,447
[feel-good music playing]

496
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:52,962
[no audible dialogue]

497
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:05,517
[heartwarming music playing]

498
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:20,698
[heartwarming music playing]

499
00:28:29,582 --> 00:28:34,212
[in unison] Thank you, Governor Diego!

500
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:39,300
-[Diego] Auntie.
-[glass shatters]

501
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:40,468
[Camia] We're going to cook--

502
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:41,553
-Ow!
-[glass shard clinks]

503
00:28:42,887 --> 00:28:43,972
[Diego] What happened?

504
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:47,058
You've got a cut.

505
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:48,476
No, it's nothing.

506
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,978
-I'll just let it bleed--
-Where's your handkerchief?

507
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:52,522
We need to cover this.
Where's your handkerchief?

508
00:28:53,732 --> 00:28:55,233
Just hold it.

509
00:28:57,485 --> 00:28:58,737
Give me your hand.

510
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:01,948
Are you okay? Does it hurt?

511
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:06,953
Remember when I also covered
your wound with a handkerchief?

512
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:10,123
[soft music playing]

513
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:15,628
Thank you.

514
00:29:18,339 --> 00:29:19,466
Let's go.

515
00:29:21,801 --> 00:29:22,886
Come on.

516
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:26,264
You go ahead. I'll just clean this up.

517
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:29,392
-Thanks again.
-[glass shards clink]

518
00:29:31,519 --> 00:29:33,855
-Chairman?
-Don't leave just yet.

519
00:29:33,938 --> 00:29:40,570
Our village prepared
a little party to thank you.

520
00:29:40,653 --> 00:29:41,613
Uh…

521
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:43,156
Friends!

522
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:45,700
They prepared a party for us.

523
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,285
-Wow!
-Wow!

524
00:29:47,368 --> 00:29:50,205
Sure thing, Chairman. We'll join you.

525
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:52,916
-Thank you, Chairman.
-Let's go!

526
00:29:53,374 --> 00:29:54,250
Okay.

527
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:57,253
-[Loring talking indistinctly]
-[laughter]

528
00:30:01,216 --> 00:30:05,428
Congressman, I hope Arnaldo's
stag party will be wholesome.

529
00:30:05,512 --> 00:30:07,764
Oh, I promise you, Ivy.

530
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:11,017
No fooling around for him.

531
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:14,062
Now, for me, that's another story.

532
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:16,189
-Ma.
-I know!

533
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:18,817
Arnaldo, relax. I'll take care of Ivy.

534
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:21,277
She's going to be okay. Let's go?

535
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:22,403
Come on.

536
00:30:23,404 --> 00:30:24,531
-Let's go.
-[Ivy] Behave.

537
00:30:24,614 --> 00:30:26,783
[Arnaldo] Of course. Always.

538
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:31,788
Chairman, thank you very much
for warmly welcoming us here.

539
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:33,289
I'll make sure

540
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:35,500
that if I become the governor
of this province,

541
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:38,878
this place will become
prosperous and thriving.

542
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:42,465
We'd just like to ask you a favor.

543
00:30:42,549 --> 00:30:44,551
If we ever find ourselves in need of aid

544
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:46,135
from the citizens of Ardiente,

545
00:30:47,303 --> 00:30:49,722
we hope we can count on your village.

546
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:51,933
You can count on us, Mr. Torillo.

547
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:55,311
Thank you, Chairman.

548
00:30:57,188 --> 00:30:58,773
Well, what are we waiting for?

549
00:30:58,857 --> 00:30:59,941
Let's dig in.

550
00:31:00,775 --> 00:31:03,361
Come on! Let's eat, friends!

551
00:31:03,444 --> 00:31:05,697
-[Marlon] Let's go, Batch!
-[Diego] Auntie, eat up.

552
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:07,323
-Is it good?
-So good.

553
00:31:07,407 --> 00:31:09,158
[indistinct chatter]

554
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:11,119
-[Diego] It's all meat dishes!
-Pork belly.

555
00:31:13,121 --> 00:31:14,497
[woman] It's yummy!

556
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:16,249
-There's a lot of food.
-[Marlon] So delicious.

557
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:20,336
It's so good!

558
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:24,173
You puked a lot that night!

559
00:31:24,257 --> 00:31:26,509
-Excuse me! Excuse me.
-We weren't able to find you.

560
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:27,927
Can I have your attention, please?

561
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:30,054
-[Arnaldo] Guys, listen up.
-Excuse me.

562
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:34,225
First and foremost, I would like to say

563
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:36,644
thank you very much to each and every one

564
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:41,024
for coming on such short notice.
Thank you very much.

565
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:43,818
Congressman, we'll make sure

566
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:47,113
that this will be a memorable
night for Arnaldo, of course!

567
00:31:47,196 --> 00:31:50,408
-Okay! I'll be expecting that.
-That's good to hear.

568
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:53,453
And on that note,
I'd like to propose a toast.

569
00:31:53,536 --> 00:31:57,540
For Arnaldo! For his marriage,

570
00:31:57,624 --> 00:32:01,336
for his success. Viva Ardiente!

571
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:02,795
[in unison] Viva Ardiente!

572
00:32:04,964 --> 00:32:06,716
[tense music playing]

573
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:10,428
Hey! We all wore white

574
00:32:10,511 --> 00:32:13,723
because I thought
the theme was "all white."

575
00:32:13,806 --> 00:32:15,183
I'm sorry, Ivy.

576
00:32:15,266 --> 00:32:19,562
I completely forgot all about
that and ended up wearing red.

577
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:21,689
I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you.

578
00:32:21,773 --> 00:32:24,067
Just look at what I prepared for you.

579
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:27,820
Let's welcome my future daughter-in-law,

580
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:31,324
-Ms. Ivy Aguas, our bride-to-be!
-[applause]

581
00:32:31,407 --> 00:32:34,535
We're going to have fun tonight!
A really fun, fun night!

582
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:35,995
Shall we?

583
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:37,038
Let's go?

584
00:32:37,121 --> 00:32:39,123
[tense music playing]

585
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:44,587
[Emilia] Ivy, come! Look!

586
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,298
We have our own bartender!

587
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:49,801
And then, I got the whole place for you!

588
00:32:51,219 --> 00:32:54,806
Isn't it great? Hey, friends! How are you?

589
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:58,935
Get some alcohol, okay?
Get loaded tonight! It's on me!

590
00:32:59,894 --> 00:33:03,189
Get some alcohol, okay?
The booze is on me!

591
00:33:04,023 --> 00:33:04,941
Hi.

592
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:07,777
Friends!

593
00:33:07,860 --> 00:33:11,072
What are you doing there?
Get some drinks and load up!

594
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:16,244
Ivy, what are you doing there?
Join me here.

595
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:20,790
[tense music playing]

596
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:28,089
Oh, Ivy. You look so bored!

597
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:32,135
We should have fun, right?

598
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:33,636
Hmm? Right?

599
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:40,435
So, is this part of your plan, Emilia?

600
00:33:42,311 --> 00:33:44,689
Okay. Let's have fun!

601
00:33:46,024 --> 00:33:47,900
-[water splashing]
-[yelps]

602
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:50,486
[upbeat music playing]

603
00:33:54,782 --> 00:33:55,616
[exhales]

604
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,703
[laughing]

605
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:00,246
[laughs]

606
00:34:00,329 --> 00:34:01,873
Are you okay, Emilia?

607
00:34:01,956 --> 00:34:03,958
I'm okay! How about you, Ivy?

608
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:06,794
Are you okay? You look a little cold.

609
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:09,130
I'm more than okay.

610
00:34:09,213 --> 00:34:11,924
I can keep up with any of your games.

611
00:34:12,008 --> 00:34:15,136
How about you? Are you ready
for what I'm about to do?

612
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:18,014
[giggles]

613
00:34:18,097 --> 00:34:21,225
Let's have some fun! Let's go get a drink.

614
00:34:21,309 --> 00:34:23,186
[upbeat music playing]

615
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:27,857
-Oh!
-Oh!

616
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:29,650
-There we go!
-There you have it, dude!

617
00:34:30,151 --> 00:34:31,694
-One more! One more!
-One more!

618
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:34,489
-[man 7] Here it is, bro!
-[all shouting]

619
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:35,740
[Julio] Should I join you, guys?

620
00:34:35,823 --> 00:34:37,867
-Last one.
-[Julio] I'm just here to watch.

621
00:34:38,284 --> 00:34:39,911
-[Arnaldo] Shot! Shot! Shot!
-[man 7] This one too.

622
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:42,121
[all] Oh!

623
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:45,792
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[man 7] One more! One more!

624
00:34:47,001 --> 00:34:48,336
[men shouting]

625
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:50,713
-[man 7] One more!
-[Arnaldo] Shot! Shot! Shot!

626
00:34:50,797 --> 00:34:54,092
-Shot! Cheers!
-[men] Cheers!

627
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:55,468
[man 7] One more!

628
00:34:55,551 --> 00:34:57,303
[man whooping] There you go!

629
00:34:57,386 --> 00:34:58,930
[Arnaldo] Ah! It's so good!

630
00:34:59,806 --> 00:35:00,848
[laughing]

631
00:35:00,932 --> 00:35:02,517
[man whooping] There you go!

632
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,519
-Ah!
-[man 7] This is great!

633
00:35:04,602 --> 00:35:06,062
[Arnaldo] Oh, man. Thank you. Thank you.

634
00:35:06,145 --> 00:35:07,021
Thank you.

635
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:10,608
[instrumental music playing]

636
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:12,944
[exhales sharply]

637
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:17,448
Oh, my goodness, Emilia! Ivy!

638
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:21,994
My goodness!
You two should fix yourselves.

639
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:24,163
Why did you suddenly jump in the pool?!

640
00:35:24,247 --> 00:35:25,998
You're not even dressed for it!

641
00:35:26,082 --> 00:35:27,208
-Thanks, Mamita.
-Well, Auntie,

642
00:35:27,291 --> 00:35:29,794
that's just how
my daughter-in-law and I play.

643
00:35:29,877 --> 00:35:32,588
-Right, Ivy? [gasps]
-You're so silly, Emilia! Sorry.

644
00:35:32,672 --> 00:35:33,673
-Not again.
-[Claire] Oh, you guys!

645
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:34,882
Sorry.

646
00:35:34,966 --> 00:35:36,509
Come on. Get up.

647
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:40,721
[whooping]

648
00:35:42,223 --> 00:35:43,224
[exhales]

649
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:54,193
[Claire] Can I get that, please?

650
00:35:55,903 --> 00:35:56,946
Emilia.

651
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:59,490
-Thank you.
-Wear this robe. Ivy.

652
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:01,075
Thanks, Mamita.

653
00:36:06,247 --> 00:36:07,498
Well, girls!

654
00:36:07,582 --> 00:36:10,793
Since we're all wet, let's have fun!

655
00:36:10,877 --> 00:36:14,755
We need something to warm us up! Boys!

656
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:18,509
[upbeat party music playing]

657
00:37:02,845 --> 00:37:05,097
[sinister music playing]

658
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:31,165
[instrumental music playing]

659
00:37:40,841 --> 00:37:42,093
[Ivy] Thank goodness, it's over.

660
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:43,761
Ivy, have some.

661
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:49,725
-For me?
-Yeah.

662
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:55,106
Oh, thank you, Emilia. But I'm good.

663
00:37:55,773 --> 00:37:57,108
Come on.

664
00:37:57,191 --> 00:37:59,694
Don't be such a party pooper.
Have a drink.

665
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:04,532
Well, I promised Arnaldo
I wouldn't get drunk tonight.

666
00:38:05,408 --> 00:38:10,037
Wow! Ivy, I made this
especially for you. I insist.

667
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:12,707
Emilia, I'm getting married soon.

668
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:14,917
And I don't want your son and I to fight

669
00:38:15,001 --> 00:38:16,585
just because I got drunk.

670
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:21,549
I'm just trying to be a good
girlfriend, I mean, fiancée.

671
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:22,800
What?

672
00:38:25,636 --> 00:38:28,347
-[all] Shot! Shot! Shot!
-[indistinct chatter]

673
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:29,849
[man 7] Three!

674
00:38:29,932 --> 00:38:32,435
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[indistinct shouting]

675
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:35,271
[whooping, shouting]

676
00:38:35,354 --> 00:38:36,605
Yeah!

677
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:38,691
That's some tolerance you got there, bro.

678
00:38:38,774 --> 00:38:41,027
Looks like Miss Aguas is in for it

679
00:38:41,110 --> 00:38:43,362
once you let loose on your honeymoon.

680
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:45,614
-[whooping, laughter]
-Ha!

681
00:38:45,698 --> 00:38:47,908
Ha! Ha!

682
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:51,120
-Are you insulting Ivy?!
-No, man.

683
00:38:51,203 --> 00:38:53,289
-What?
-Hey, bro. Calm down.

684
00:38:53,372 --> 00:38:56,292
It's all about fun tonight.

685
00:38:56,375 --> 00:38:59,086
No fighting, okay? Chill a bit.
Let's just drink.

686
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,464
[man 7] Why don't we show him
our surprise?

687
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:02,923
-[man 8] Okay. Okay.
-[man 7] Come on.

688
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:05,343
[Arnaldo] What surprise? Will I like this?

689
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:07,803
You bet, bro. Trust me.

690
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:09,263
-[Arnaldo] All right.
-Here it is.

691
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:15,061
Over here. Sit here, Mayor.
Just relax, Mayor. Sit here.

692
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:16,312
[Arnaldo] This better not be a prank.

693
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:19,774
No. Why would we do that?
Just sit here. There you go.

694
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:21,108
[laughing]

695
00:39:21,650 --> 00:39:24,111
[man 8] Best man, you blindfold him.

696
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:25,738
Relax, Mayor. Relax.

697
00:39:25,821 --> 00:39:27,907
What is this? If this is
just some dumb trick--

698
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:30,534
[man 8] Chill out. You'll see. Game!

699
00:39:31,243 --> 00:39:32,953
[tense music playing]

700
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:36,582
[men whooping]

701
00:39:36,665 --> 00:39:41,045
[Arnaldo] I'm nervous.
What are we going to do?

702
00:39:41,128 --> 00:39:44,924
-Oh, goodness!
-[man 8] Way to go, Congressman!

703
00:39:45,841 --> 00:39:49,720
[man 7] Awesome choice, bro!
You got good taste in chicks.

704
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:51,514
Very nice choice!

705
00:39:51,972 --> 00:39:54,266
-[man 8] Here she comes!
-[whooping]

706
00:39:56,185 --> 00:39:58,646
[man 8] All right, it's Mayor's turn!

707
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:01,649
[laughing]

708
00:40:01,732 --> 00:40:03,984
Hey, I still have meetings tomorrow!

709
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:05,236
[man 8] This is great!

710
00:40:05,319 --> 00:40:07,822
[suspenseful music playing]

711
00:40:08,697 --> 00:40:09,490
[man whooping]

712
00:40:10,408 --> 00:40:12,743
-Whoa!
-There!

713
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:16,122
-[man whistles]
-[man 7] I think he's in love.

714
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:17,957
-[man 8] Are you okay, Mayor?
-[man 7] He's in love.

715
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:20,459
-[man 8] Are you okay, Mayor?
-Arnaldo, are you okay?

716
00:40:22,503 --> 00:40:25,005
-Can you keep up, Mayor?
-He's in love, bro. In love!

717
00:40:25,089 --> 00:40:26,132
[Julio] Mayor.

718
00:40:26,465 --> 00:40:28,884
-[man 8] Success!
-[men shouting]

719
00:40:28,968 --> 00:40:31,804
-[man 6] It's a success!
-[man 7] Cheers to the mayor!

720
00:40:31,887 --> 00:40:33,389
-[Julio] That's it, my boy!
-[man 8] Oh, man!

721
00:40:33,472 --> 00:40:35,266
-[man 7] Yeah, man!
-[Julio] Hey, hey, hey!

722
00:40:35,349 --> 00:40:36,725
Arnaldo, where are you going?

723
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:38,352
-He's going to take her home.
-I'm fine. I'm fine.

724
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,271
[indistinct shouting]

725
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:43,691
Follow him. He's had too much to drink.

726
00:40:43,774 --> 00:40:46,235
Come on! This is really good.

727
00:40:46,318 --> 00:40:47,570
Go, just have it.

728
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:49,196
[Emilia] No, I don't want
to drink tonight.

729
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,448
-I'm gonna pass.
-See?

730
00:40:50,531 --> 00:40:51,740
That makes two of us.

731
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:55,536
-So, you mixed it yourself?
-Yeah.

732
00:40:58,122 --> 00:41:00,708
Well, if neither of us wants to drink it,

733
00:41:00,791 --> 00:41:03,377
why don't you try it, Mamita?

734
00:41:04,962 --> 00:41:07,298
-Me?
-Yeah. Try it.

735
00:41:07,381 --> 00:41:10,593
-No. I already have a drink.
-It's okay. Taste it.

736
00:41:10,676 --> 00:41:12,094
Emilia made it herself.

737
00:41:12,178 --> 00:41:13,888
-[fake chuckle]
-No, thank you.

738
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:17,892
Aww. Mamita doesn't want to try it either.

739
00:41:18,684 --> 00:41:20,269
I really don't want
to drink tonight, though.

740
00:41:20,352 --> 00:41:26,358
Arnaldo and I can't fight again.
So, you have it. Thank you.

741
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:28,027
No, no, no. I'm fine.

742
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:30,362
-Thank you.
-[Ivy] Come on, don't let it go to waste.

743
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:31,822
I'll even help you. Come on.

744
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:33,699
I'm fine. I'm fine. I'm fine.

745
00:41:33,782 --> 00:41:36,827
No, come on, just a sip.

746
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:38,537
-[Claire] Oh my god.
-[Ivy] Taste it, just a little.

747
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:39,955
Say, "Ah."

748
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,874
-Come on, just a little.
-[muffled exclaim]

749
00:41:42,541 --> 00:41:44,043
[suspenseful music playing]

750
00:41:44,126 --> 00:41:45,336
[muffled exclaim]

751
00:41:46,253 --> 00:41:47,421
[gagging]

752
00:41:48,380 --> 00:41:49,256
[muffled exclaim]

753
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:52,176
[suspenseful music playing]

754
00:41:54,136 --> 00:41:55,221
Why?

755
00:42:01,852 --> 00:42:03,187
Emilia!

756
00:42:03,979 --> 00:42:05,814
[suspenseful music playing]

757
00:42:06,232 --> 00:42:08,150
[retching]

758
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:11,237
[water running]

759
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:13,489
[retching]

760
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:21,330
Emilia! Emilia!

761
00:42:23,415 --> 00:42:26,252
So, how does it feel
to fall into your own trap?

762
00:42:26,335 --> 00:42:28,796
I don't know what you're saying!
I don't know what you're saying!

763
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:30,339
Oh please, Emilia.

764
00:42:30,422 --> 00:42:33,634
Are you actually trying to play dumb?

765
00:42:33,717 --> 00:42:35,761
[coughing]

766
00:42:35,844 --> 00:42:37,471
Aunt Claire! [crying]

767
00:42:38,639 --> 00:42:40,599
[Claire] Emilia! Emilia!

768
00:42:40,683 --> 00:42:42,518
What's happening to you?!

769
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:44,687
That woman poisoned me!

770
00:42:44,770 --> 00:42:46,522
-What?!
-"Poisoned"?

771
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:50,359
This actually contained poison?

772
00:42:50,943 --> 00:42:53,070
What poison did you switch with mine?

773
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,238
-[retching]
-Oops.

774
00:42:54,321 --> 00:42:57,199
I didn't switch anything. I'm innocent.

775
00:42:57,283 --> 00:42:58,909
How the hell did you get that?!

776
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:01,328
[suspenseful music playing]

777
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:03,956
<i>I don't like this, Emilia.</i>

778
00:43:04,039 --> 00:43:06,584
<i>Your actions will only</i>
<i>get you into trouble!</i>

779
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:08,252
<i>Well, Auntie, I'd rather die</i>

780
00:43:08,335 --> 00:43:11,922
<i>than see Ivy steal everything I own.</i>

781
00:43:12,756 --> 00:43:15,050
[suspenseful music intensifies]

782
00:43:33,319 --> 00:43:37,489
It's simple, really.
I'm Ivy Aguas, remember?

783
00:43:38,657 --> 00:43:40,451
You poisoned me! [retching]

784
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:42,286
You poisoned yourself.

785
00:43:42,369 --> 00:43:46,790
Emilia, I read that this particular poison
is one of the worst.

786
00:43:46,874 --> 00:43:51,086
Your throat will constrict.

787
00:43:51,503 --> 00:43:54,381
So tight that you won't
be able to breathe!

788
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:55,966
-[wheezing]
-[Ivy] Just like that!

789
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:58,719
And then, it will make
your whole body shake!

790
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:01,764
It will make your body shake so badly
that you'll feel like passing out.

791
00:44:01,847 --> 00:44:04,099
But it will--

792
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:06,268
[Claire] Oh, gosh! You have to throw up.

793
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:08,646
You have to throw up, Emilia!
Spit out the poison!

794
00:44:08,729 --> 00:44:10,272
Do it! Hurry!

795
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:12,566
-Keep trying!
-[Emilia retching]

796
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:14,693
Put your finger in your mouth!

797
00:44:14,777 --> 00:44:16,028
That's it! Keep trying!

798
00:44:16,111 --> 00:44:18,113
[laughing]

799
00:44:18,197 --> 00:44:21,784
That's it! Come on!
Do it! Come on! Keep going!

800
00:44:21,867 --> 00:44:25,412
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[retching]

801
00:44:28,290 --> 00:44:30,751
[Arnaldo] <i>You're very beautiful, Ivy.</i>
<i>I just want to talk to you.</i>

802
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:32,753
[woman, crying]
<i>This wasn't part of the deal.</i>

803
00:44:32,836 --> 00:44:34,213
[Arnaldo] <i>Why are you giving me</i>
<i>a hard time?</i>

804
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:36,131
<i>Mayor, I'm not Ivy.</i>

805
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:37,716
<i>What are you talking about?!</i>

806
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:40,969
<i>-Reporting for duty, Mayor.</i>
<i>-Madrigal. Long time no see.</i>

807
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:42,221
<i>Just like old times, Mayor.</i>

808
00:44:42,304 --> 00:44:44,598
<i>The only difference is that</i>
<i>I work for Jaguar now.</i>

809
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:47,017
<i>He wants me to tell you</i>
<i>that your days are numbered.</i>

810
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:50,854
<i>Is this the last time we'll see</i>
<i>each other before your wedding?</i>

811
00:44:50,938 --> 00:44:55,692
[Ivy] <i>Maybe, maybe not. Thank you, Diego.</i>

812
00:44:55,776 --> 00:44:59,530
[Diego] <i>Take good care of yourself,</i>
<i>okay? Be careful.</i>

813
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:03,617
[theme music playing]
